course: dictionary
lesson: 4184
title: A giant called Goliath
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Goliath is a name from the Bible. Goliath was a giant warrior, and the young shepherd David beat him with a stone from his sling. Because of that story, a goliath (with a small g) now means something very big and strong.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «The goliath and Hercules beetles are among the biggest insects.» The word biggest is the clue: a goliath is something huge. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The huge beetles are among the biggest insects." It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Sometimes a goliath is beaten by something smaller. The story of David and Goliath teaches that courage and faith can beat size and strength. Sports reporters say «a David and Goliath match» when a tiny team plays a famous, much stronger one. The tiny team is the David; the big one is the goliath.
fact: Goliath was a giant warrior in the Bible, killed by the young shepherd David with a stone from his sling.
fact: A goliath (small g) is a very big, strong person, company or thing, often one that is beaten by a smaller one.
fact: «A David and Goliath match» means a small team playing a famous, much bigger one.
fact: «The goliath frog of Cameroon and Equatorial Guinea is the biggest frog in the world.» It is about 32 centimetres long.
fact: «The Goliath birdeater is the heaviest spider in the world», with a leg span like a dinner plate.
exercise: «A tiny team beat the famous champions. It was a David and Goliath match.» In this sentence, what does Goliath stand for? | *The famous, much bigger team | The tiny team | The referee | The crowd in the stands
exercise: «The goliath frog of Cameroon is the biggest frog in the world.» What does biggest tell you about the goliath frog? | It is the same size as a bird | *It is huge, far bigger than other frogs | It is a small, quiet frog | It lives high up in a tree
exercise: Courage is not having no fear; it is doing what is right even when you are afraid, like David facing Goliath. What does this story teach us? | Big people always win | Stones are the best weapon | Shepherds should never fight | *Courage and faith can beat size and strength
test: «He runs a goliath of a company.» What does goliath mean here? | A short story | A tiny shop on the corner | A quiet lake | *A very big, powerful company
test: Who killed Goliath in the Bible story? | A wise old teacher | *A young shepherd called David | A king | A giant
exam: In «Goliath was a giant warrior», which word is a proper noun, a name for one special person? | *Goliath | giant | warrior | a
